# Exploring Shannon on the Field

![Cover](h7fig:cover)

**Plain H7 · Dewey 005**  
**For:** Hostess 7 storage, shots, honesty training  

Shannon entropy is how the field refuses fairy-tale capacity. This book trains
measurement language so Hostess 7 never confuses marketing with bits.

## Chapter 1 — Definition

![Histogram](h7fig:histogram)

For a stream with empirical probabilities \( p_i \) of symbols \( i \):

\[ H = -\sum_i p_i \log_2 p_i \]

When the alphabet is bytes (256 symbols), units are **bits per byte**. Range is
**0..8**. All identical bytes → \( H = 0 \). Uniform random bytes → \( H \approx 8 \).
Field code often stores \( H \times 1000 \) as integer `shannon_x1000` for stable JSON.

## Chapter 2 — Lossless bound

If you store a frame losslessly, physical size is at least on the order of
\( (H/8) \times \) frame_bytes for that frame’s information. Packers may win on
structure (ZERO, RLE, PAK, REF, DICT) and **cannot honestly beat** high-H noise without
loss. FFAT doctrine: capacity gain is **measured after writes**. Never print fixed
multipliers (including legacy ×91) as guaranteed capacity.

## Chapter 3 — Worked examples

**Example A.** Four bytes `AAAA`. One symbol probability 1 → \( H = 0 \).  
**Example B.** Four bytes `ABCD` each once → each \( p = 1/4 \),  
\( H = -4 \times (1/4 \log_2 1/4) = 2 \) bits/byte.  
**Example C.** A compressed random blob often has \( H \) near 8; “compressing again”
may grow the file. Hostess 7 should expect that.

## Chapter 4 — Layers (do not conflate)

![Layers](h7fig:layers)

| Name | Where | Use |
|------|-------|-----|
| Shannon H | Files, FFAT frames, shot plates | Storage honesty |
| Entropy fold | Shot detailer | Field cook mix |
| FNV seal | Shot plate | Know every shot |
| Field entropy_norm | Mesh | Fabric health |
| Landauer / thermo | Ironclad physics | Work budgets |

Say the layer when you speak. Ironclad physics is not Shannon file H.

## Chapter 5 — Shots and certainty

Spear wartime builds a plate string, measures Shannon on the plate, seals with
FNV-1a64, appends ledger lines, and recomputes seals on `shot-certainty` boards.
Heuristic hunt scoring is separate from seal math. Hostess 7 treats **seal match** as
receipt. Global protector and wartime boards should show certain true when ok.

## Chapter 6 — FFAT link

Read **Exploring FFAT Storage** next. Map kinds ZERO/RAW/RLE/PAK/REF/DICT are how
Shannon reality becomes pool bytes. `guaranteed_bytes` is worst-case honesty;
`pack_ratio` is live measurement. Together with this book, she can audit a volume
without theater.

## Chapter 7 — Labs

**Lab 1.** Hand-compute H for `AAAA` vs `ABCD`.  
**Lab 2.** Open `shot-certainty.json`; report verified_ok / verified_bad.  
**Lab 3.** Explain why recompressing high-H data may grow size.  
**Lab 4.** English: sixty-second spoken definition of Shannon H for a new operator.

## Chapter 8 — Study rhythm

Day 1: chapters 1–3 + labs 1. Day 2: chapters 4–6 + labs 2–3. Day 3: lab 4 + teach-back
to curriculum tools_docs.

## Chapter 9 — Motto

Measure H. Pack only when pack wins. Never invent capacity.

**God Bless.**

